            <ArticleTitle>[Hemopericardium caused by endocarditis ulcerosa: an unusual cause of sudden death in adolescence].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>158-66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report on the case of a 18-year-old student who died suddenly and unexpectedly of a pericardial tamponade after perforated ulcer-polypous endocarditis of the aortic valve. The detection of aerococcus urinae--which usually causes urinary tract infection--on the inflamed aortic valve demonstrates an unusual pathogenetic chain linking complexes of findings in the urogenital system and the heart.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
